# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Oasis Construction — environment
#
# Copy to .env.local for development, or set the same variables in the hosting
# provider's dashboard for production. Never commit real values.
#
# Everything here is optional. With none of it set the site builds, renders and
# is fully browsable; the quote form is the one thing that needs configuration
# before launch, and until it has some it tells the visitor to phone instead of
# reporting a message as sent that nobody received.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------


# === 1. Form delivery — REQUIRED BEFORE LAUNCH =============================
#
# The three forms all post to /api/contact. Until one of the two providers
# below is configured the endpoint returns 503 and the visitor is shown the
# phone and email fallback.

# Option A — Resend (recommended). Create a key at https://resend.com/api-keys
# and verify the sending domain before going live.
RESEND_API_KEY=
# Where quote requests are delivered. Comma-separated for several recipients.
CONTACT_TO_EMAIL=contact@oasis-construction.ca
# Must be an address on a domain verified with Resend.
CONTACT_FROM_EMAIL=soumissions@oasis-construction.ca

# Option B — any HTTPS endpoint that accepts a JSON POST (Make, Zapier, n8n, a
# CRM webhook…). Used only when the Resend variables above are absent.
# Photo attachments are listed by name but not uploaded through this path, so
# prefer Resend if the business wants to see the photos in the email.
CONTACT_WEBHOOK_URL=


# === 2. Measurement ========================================================
#
# Set GTM *or* GA4, not both — with a container id present the site loads GTM
# only and expects GA4 to be configured inside it. The production Google Ads
# base tag is installed in the document head and starts in denied Consent Mode;
# the events below are still pushed to window.dataLayer for verification.
#
# Events include form_lead, form_submit, the guided-form funnel, phone_click,
# cta_click, scroll_depth, faq_expand, external_link_click and page_view.

NEXT_PUBLIC_GTM_ID=GTM-WSXTTT7R
NEXT_PUBLIC_GA4_ID=

# Google Ads conversion tracking.
#
# Both values come from Google Ads > Goals > Conversions > the conversion
# action > "Tag setup" > "Install the tag yourself". The snippet Google shows
# contains them: send_to: 'AW-1234567890/AbC-D_efGhIjKl'  ->  the part before
# the slash is the id, the part after is the label.
#
# Set BOTH or neither. The id alone loads the tag and counts nothing; the
# label alone has nowhere to send. Every form on the site (quote, contact and
# the guided funnel) fires this conversion once, on a lead that was actually
# delivered - never on a failed submit, and never for a visitor who declined.
#
# Leave these empty when NEXT_PUBLIC_GTM_ID is set: with a container present
# the site loads GTM only, and the conversion tag belongs inside the container,
# triggered on the `form_submit` dataLayer event. Filling in both would count
# every lead twice.
NEXT_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_ADS_ID=
NEXT_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_ADS_LEAD_LABEL=

# Meta Pixel. Install now, activate when the ads launch.
NEXT_PUBLIC_META_PIXEL_ID=

# Consent. Nothing above is loaded until the visitor accepts the Law 25
# banner: no GTM, no gtag.js, no pixel, no request to a third party at all.
# Consent Mode v2 defaults ride along anyway (denied, with ads_data_redaction
# on and url_passthrough enabled so a gclid survives internal navigation), so
# a container configured for consent mode behaves if one is ever added.
#
# The trade: Google's own recommendation is to load the tags under a denial
# and let Consent Mode redact them, which is what earns modelled conversions.
# That would contradict what the banner tells the visitor, so the site does
# not do it. Changing that is a decision for the business, not a default -
# see the `granted &&` guards in src/components/Analytics.tsx.


# === 3. Spam protection (optional) =========================================
#
# The forms already carry a honeypot field, a minimum fill time and a per-IP
# rate limit. reCAPTCHA v3 is the extra layer for a determined attack.
# Both variables must be set for it to activate; either one alone is ignored,
# so a half-finished setup can never silently reject real leads.
# Keys: https://www.google.com/recaptcha/admin (choose v3)

NEXT_PUBLIC_RECAPTCHA_SITE_KEY=
RECAPTCHA_SECRET_KEY=
